          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Given
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} categories
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            %strong functor category
            – written
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi D
                    %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D^C
            or
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [C,D]
            – is the category whose
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/class"} class
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
                is the collection of all
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functors"} functors
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi C
                      %mo →
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \colon C \to D
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
                are
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformations"} natural transformations
                between these functors.
          %h3#in_homotopy_type_theory In homotopy type theory
          %p
            Discussion in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
          %p
            Note: the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/HoTT+book"} HoTT book
            calls a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+category+in+HoTT"} internal category in HoTT
            a “precategory” and a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalent+category"} univalent category
            a “category”, but here we shall refer to the standard terminology of “category” and “univalent category” respectively.
          %p
            For
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A,B
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi B
                      %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B^A
            = succeed "," do
              %strong functor category
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi B
                      %mi A
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (B^A)_0
              is the type of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functors"} functors
              from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              to
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi hom
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi B
                          %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo ,
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} hom_{B^A}(F,G)
              is the type of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformations"} natural transformations
              from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              to
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %p
            %strong Proof.
            We define
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mi F
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi a
                    %mo ≡
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                        %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (1_F)_a \equiv 1_{F a}
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi γ
                  %mo :
                  %mi F
                  %mo →
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma : F \to G
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi δ
                    %mo :
                    %mi G
                    %mo →
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta : G \to H
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi δ
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi γ
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi a
                    %mo ≡
                    %msub
                      %mi δ
                      %mi a
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mi γ
                      %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\delta \circ \gamma)_a \equiv \delta_a \circ \gamma_a
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi B
                    %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B^A
            follow from those for
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo □
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \square
          %p
            We define a
            %strong natural isomorphism
            to be an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi B
                      %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B^A
          %h2#usage Usage
          %p
            Functor categories serve as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-categories"} hom-categories
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+2-category"} strict 2-category
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
          %p
            In the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category+theory"} enriched category theory
            the functor category is generalized to the
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+functor+category"} enriched functor category
          %p
            In the absence of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
            (including many
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+category"} internal
            situations), the appropriate notion to use is often instead the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anafunctor+category"} anafunctor category
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#limits_and_colimits_and_closure Limits and colimits and closure
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            has
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits"} limits
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
            of a certain shape, then so does
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [C,D]
            and they are computed pointwise. (However, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            is not complete, then other limits in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [C,D]
            can exist “by accident” without being pointwise.)
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is small and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+category"} cartesian closed
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complete+category"} complete
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [C,D]
            is cartesian closed. See at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+category"} cartesian closed category
            for a proof.
          %h3#LocalPresentability Accessibility and local presentability
          %p
            Functor categories enjoy the following accessibility and local presentability properties, as explained by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Zhen+Lin+Low"} Zhen Lin Low
            at
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "http://nforum.mathforge.org/discussion/6152"} nForum
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
                \-
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/accessible+functors"} accessible functors
                from a
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi κ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/accessible+category"} accessible category
                to any accessible category form an accessible category. (It is not so easy to say what the accessibility rank is here.)
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
                \-accessible functors from a
                = succeed "-accessible" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi κ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi λ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+category"} presentable category
                form a locally
                = succeed "-presentable" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi λ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
            %li
              %p
                Cocontinuous functors between
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+categories"} locally presentable categories
                form a locally presentable category. More precisely, if
                = succeed "\u00A0and\u00A0" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
                are locally
                = succeed "-presentable," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi κ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi C
                        %mo ,
                        %mi D
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [C,D]
            %li
              %p
                Continuous accessible functors between locally presentable categories form the opposite of a locally presentable category. More precisely, if
                = succeed "\u00A0and\u00A0" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
                are locally
                = succeed "-presentable," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi κ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi C
                        %mo ,
                        %mi D
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} rm
                            %mi op
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [C,D]^{\rm op}
          %p
            Indeed, the point is this: given a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/accessible+category"} accessible category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mi Ind
                    %mi κ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒜
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C} \simeq Ind^\kappa (\mathcal{A})
            (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
            essentially small), the category of
            = succeed "-accessible" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝒟
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C} \to \mathcal{D}
            (for arbitrary
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒟
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}
            = succeed "-accessible\u201D" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            = succeed "-filtered" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒟
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A} \to \mathcal{D}
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒟
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}
                is accessible, then so is
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi 𝒜
                        %mo ,
                        %mi 𝒟
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\mathcal{A}, \mathcal{D}]
            %li#FunctorsIntoLocallyPresCatAreLocallyPres
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒜
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
                is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒟
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}
                is locally
                = succeed "-presentable," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi λ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi 𝒜
                      %mo ,
                      %mi 𝒟
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\mathcal{A}, \mathcal{D}]
                is locally presentable.
            %li
              %p
                Colimit-preserving functors out of a locally
                = succeed "-presentable" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi κ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
                = succeed "-accessible." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi κ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            %li
              %p
                A right adjoint between locally
                = succeed "-presentable" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi κ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
                = succeed "-accessible" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi κ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
                = succeed "-accessible" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi κ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
                = succeed "-presentable" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi κ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
                = succeed "-filtered" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi κ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
          %p
            Statement 2 is
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#AdámekRosický94"} Adámek &amp; Rosický (1994), Cor. 1.54
          %p
            In general, accessible functors between accessible categories do not form an accessible category due to size issues. The best one can hope for is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/class-accessible+category"} class-accessible category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            be an accessible category that is
            %em not
            essentially small. Consider the category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
            of all accessible functors
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C} \to \mathbf{Set}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo ,
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\mathcal{C}, \mathbf{Set}]
            containing all representable functors and closed under small colimits. In particular,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
            is accessible if and only if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
            locally presentable. We claim
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
            is not accessible.
          %p
            Indeed, suppose
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
            has a small generating family, say
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒢
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{G}
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒢
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{G}
            is
            = succeed "-accessible." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C} (X, -)
            for some object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            that is
            %em not
            = succeed "-presentable." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            exists because
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            is
            %em not
            essentially small.) Since
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒢
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{G}
            generates, there is a small diagram of
            = succeed "-accessible" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C} (X, -)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C} (X, -)
            is a retract of a
            = succeed "-accessible" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            = succeed "-accessible:" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/class-locally+presentable+category"} class-locally presentable category
          %h3#in_homotopy_type_theory_2 In homotopy type theory
          %h4#lemma_924 Lemma 9.2.4
          %p
            A natural transformation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi γ
                  %mo :
                  %mi F
                  %mo →
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma : F \to G
            is an isomorphism in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi B
                    %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B^A
            if and only if each
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi γ
                    %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma_a
            is an isomorphism in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
          %p
            %strong Proof.
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi γ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma
            is an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi δ
                  %mo :
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta : G \to F
            that is its inverse. By definition of composition in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi B
                      %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B^A
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi δ
                    %mi γ
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi a
                    %mo ≡
                    %msub
                      %mi δ
                      %mi a
                    %msub
                      %mi γ
                      %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\delta \gamma)_a \equiv \delta_a \gamma_a
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi δ
                  %mi γ
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mn 1
                    %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta \gamma = 1_F
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi γ
                  %mi δ
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mn 1
                    %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma \delta=1_G
            imply that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi δ
                    %mi a
                  %msub
                    %mi γ
                    %mi a
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mn 1
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta_a \gamma_a = 1_{F a}
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi γ
                      %mi a
                    %msub
                      %mi δ
                      %mi a
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                        %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma_a \delta_a = 1_{G a}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi γ
                    %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma_a
            is an isomorphism.
          %p
            Conversely, suppose each
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi γ
                    %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma_a
            is an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi δ
                      %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta_a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi δ
                  %mo :
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta : G \to F
            with components
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi δ
                      %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta_a
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mi f
                  %mo ∘
                  %msub
                    %mi δ
                    %mi a
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi δ
                    %mi b
                  %mo ∘
                  %msub
                    %mi γ
                    %mi b
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi F
                  %mi f
                  %mo ∘
                  %msub
                    %mi δ
                    %mi a
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi δ
                    %mi b
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi G
                  %mi f
                  %mo ∘
                  %msub
                    %mi γ
                    %mi a
                  %mo ∘
                  %msub
                    %mi δ
                    %mi a
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi δ
                    %mi b
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi G
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F f \circ \delta_a=\delta_b \circ \gamma_b \circ F f \circ \delta_a = \delta_b \circ G f \circ \gamma_a \circ \delta_a = \delta_b \circ G f
          %p
            Now since composition and identity of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformations"} natural transformations
            is determined on their components, we have
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi γ
                  %mi δ
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mn 1
                    %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma \delta=1_G
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi δ
                  %mi γ
                  %msub
                    %mn 1
                    %mi F
                  %mo .
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo □
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta \gamma 1_F.\ \square
          %h4#theorem_925 Theorem 9.2.5
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalent+category"} univalent category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi B
                    %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B^A
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalent+category"} univalent category
          %p
            %strong Proof.
            Let
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo ,
                    %mi G
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F,G:A\to B
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi idtoiso
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi F
                  %mo =
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi F
                  %mo ≅
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} idtoiso:({F}={G}) \to (F\cong G)
            is an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence"} equivalence
          %p
            To give an inverse to it, suppose
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi γ
                  %mo :
                  %mi F
                  %mo ≅
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma:F\cong G
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a:A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi γ
                      %mi a
                    %mo :
                    %mi F
                    %mi a
                    %mo ≅
                    %mi G
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma_a:F a \cong G a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity"} identity
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi isotoid
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi γ
                      %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mi a
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                      %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} isotoid(\gamma_a):{F a}={G a}
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+extensionality"} function extensionality
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity"} identity
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi γ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %mo :
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi F
                        %mn 0
                    %msub
                      %mo =
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mn 0
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi B
                          %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi G
                        %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar{\gamma}:{F_0}=_{(A_0\to B_0)}{G_0}
          %p
            Now since the last two axioms of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            are
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mere+propositions"} mere propositions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo =
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {F}={G}
            it will suffice to show that for any
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a,b:A
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi hom
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi hom
                    %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi F
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi F
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_{a,b}:hom_A(a,b) \to hom_B(F a,F b)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi hom
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi hom
                    %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi G
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_{a,b}:hom_A(a,b) \to hom_B(G a,G b)
          %p
            become equal when
            %span.newWikiWord
              transported
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/transported"} ?
            along
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi γ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar\gamma
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+extensionality"} function extensionality
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar\gamma
            becomes equal to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi isotoid
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi γ
                      %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} isotoid(\gamma_a)
          .query
            %p
              This reference needs to be included. For now as transports are not yet written up I didn’t bother including a reference to the page
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalent+category"} univalent category
          %p
            But by [INCLUDE ME],
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transporting"} transporting
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi hom
                    %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi F
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi F
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F f:hom_B(F a,F b)
            along
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi isotoid
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi γ
                    %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} isotoid(\gamma_a)
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi isotoid
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi γ
                    %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} isotoid(\gamma_b)
            is equal to the composite
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi γ
                      %mi b
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi F
                    %mi f
                    %mo ∘
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} inv
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi γ
                        %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma_b\circ F f\circ \inv{(\gamma_a)}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi γ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma
            is equal to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G f
          %p
            This completes the definition of a function
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo ≅
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo =
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (F\cong G) \to (F =G)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi F
                  %mo =
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi F
                  %mo ≅
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi F
                  %mo =
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (F= G) \to (F\cong G) \to (F =G).
          %p
            Since hom-sets are
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+types"} identity types
            are
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mere+propositions"} mere propositions
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identities"} identities
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo ,
                  %mi q
                  %mo :
                  %mi F
                  %mo =
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p,q:F =G
            are equal, it suffices to show that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %msub
                      %mo =
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi F
                            %mn 0
                        %mo =
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi G
                            %mn 0
                    %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p =_{{F_0}={G_0}}{q}
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi γ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar\gamma
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi γ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma
            were of the form
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi idtoiso
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
